(x) To post all proceedings before the Court after service of notice is complete, where notice has been ordered, except matters where there is a specific order of the Court to post the same on an earlier or specific date;
(xi) To post a proceeding in court before the completion of service of notice, on filing of an application requesting judicial orders;
(xii) To order notice to the respondent/respondents and the Government Pleader on an application for permission to sue as indigent;
(xi) To dispense with notice to party respondents in Motor Accidents Claims Appeal, wherein the insurance company has appeared and admitted their liability;
(xiv) To allow applications filed for impleading proforma party/ parties, provided there is no objection from the parties already in the party array;
(xv) To allow application for impleading legal representatives of deceased party, provided it is filed within the time prescribed by law and is not opposed, and if opposed, record reasons and post the application before court;
(xvi) To order notice on application filed under Order XXII sub-rule (2) of rule 9 of the Code and to allow the same after the notice is served, provided the same is not opposed, and if opposed, record reasons and post the application before court;(3)
(xvii) To order notice on the application filed under section 5 of the Limitation Act, 1963, to condone the delay in filing an application under Order XXlII Rule 9 of the Code and to allow the same after the notice is served, provided the same is not opposed and if opposed, record reasons and post the application before court;
(xvi) To note abatement of any proceedings after the expiry of the period prescribed by law and post it before the Court;
(xix) To pass orders on all Interlocutory Applications which are unopposed and are of a formal nature;
(xx) To permit or require any party to offer evidence by affidavit with respect to any application or matter which he is empowered to act under these rules;
