(xxxi) To pass orders on applications for exemption from paying court fees or extension of time for paying court fees, if provided under these Rules or the Kerala Court Fees and Suits Valuation Act, 1959 or for furnishing undertaking, bank guarantee or security, subject to a maximum period of 60 days. The Registrar (Case and Court Management) shall, if the court fees, undertaking, bank guarantee or security is not paid/furnished within the time so fixed or extended, record reasons and place the matter before Court;
(xxxi) To adjudicate applications for refund of court fees under these Rules or under the Kerala Court Fees and Suits Valuation Act, 1959 or under any notification if issued thereunder and to order refund of court fee paid by mistake or inadvertence;
(xxxiv) To pass orders on all applications for impleading/ substitution of legal heirs of accused/complainant/victim in criminal proceedings wherein such applications are filed within time and are legally permissible and not opposed. However, in appropriate cases, the Registrar (Case and Court Management) may place the matter before the Court with a report;
(xxxv) To refer the parties to mediation on mutual agreement;
(xxxvi) To pass appropriate orders for renewal of bank guarantees, fixed deposit receipts and other deposits made under the orders of Court;
(xxxvii) To list before the Registrar (Case and Court Management), all bail applications, arbitration requests, transfer petitions, contempt of court cases, restoration petitions, review petitions, and such other category of cases as may be decided by the High Court from time to time, which are pending for more than 6 months or such other period as may be decided by the High Court, and to post those cases for hearing before the Bench concerned. The Registrar (Case and Court Management) shall list and post for hearing before the Bench concerned, all other categories of cases, in accordance with the timeline fixed by the High Court for the respective categories of cases or based on the exigency of the matter;
(xxxvi) To implement any scheme for case and court management, intelligent listing of cases using Artificial Intelligence(Al) tool/s approved by the State Case Management System Committee (SCMSC) and the Full Court.".
